tests/test_store_writes.py (8 tests, of which 3 are new for the move path) proves: tasks move of task A commits only that task's old and new state paths while task B's pending edit stays uncommitted; after a move the store has nothing pending for the moved task - no .ops/staging/<task> leftover and no old-state-folder deletion (git show --no-renames); the two-agent case leaves B still pending and A fully committed. Full suite: 131 passed; the only 4 failures are test_robustness cases failing identically on unmodified main (task 326); ruff adds no new errors. tasks undo is a pre-existing silent no-op (verified on main) - its store write is now scoped the same way, but undo itself needs its own task.